      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comments inline, but I don\u0027t know enough about finalization, reachabilityFence and @ReachabilitySensitive to comment on whether this is correct.\n\nHans, would you be a good person to look at this? As you can probably tell from the code, this is an utility class that maps a filedescriptor (stored as an int). The purpose of this CL is to prevent filedescriptor leaks even if the user forgets to call close() explicitly.\n\nPerhaps unrelated to the above question: filedescriptors have the known problem that as soon as close is called once on a given fd, the fd int becomes available to use by any other code in the process, so close must not be called a second time or it could close someone else\u0027s fd. Not sure if this can be done safely in the absence of explicit synchronization such that the close() call and the write to mFdInt (or whatever variable tracks whether close() was called) are in the same synchronized block.",
      "revId": "c29e1e24aaf9aef87b5b218a6aa4eac77152d2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
